=====================================================


What is it?
===========

risky is a little-endian RISC-V emulator written in C99,
based on (Asami's book)[https://github.com/d0iasm/rvemu-for-book].

It was built for learning purposes and is not intended to be used
seriously.

See LICENSE for license details.

Building
========

To build risky you just need POSIX libc and make implementations.
In most cases you can just do:

	$ make

And to install it:

	# make install

Running it
==========

Run risky with a RISC-V assembly file to run it.

For more information refer to the manpage.
